Done. Here's a summary of the changes:

**Bug**: When the `else` branch of an `else if` chain contained only a comment (no expression), the `build_cond` function produced `true -> # comment` — a comment right after `->` means no clause expression, causing `TokenMissingError`.

**Fix** (2 changes to `lib/syntax/no_else_if.ex`):

1. **`build_cond/3`** (line 163): Added `Enum.split_with(clean_body, &(not comment?(&1)))` to separate expression lines from comment-only lines. When `expr_lines` is empty but there are trailing comments, it inserts `nil` as the clause expression and preserves comments on indented lines below. When both expressions and comments exist, comments are appended after the expression lines.

2. **`comment?/1`** (line 212): New helper predicate — `Regex.match?(~r/^\s*#/, line)`.

**Tests added** (3 new in `test/syntax/no_else_if_fix_test.exs`):
- `"fixes else branch with comment-only body (inserts nil)"` — exact output match
- `"comment-only else fix is well-formed (parses)"` — `valid_syntax?` check
- `"comment-only else fix no longer flags"` — `analyze(fix(...)) == []` check

All 8 tests pass (5 existing + 3 new).[0m
